# init service for sud (the root daemon).
#
# seclabel is REQUIRED here even though this device runs SELinux Permissive.
# AOSP pie init (system/core/init/service.cpp, ComputeContextFromExecutable)
# rejects a service whose executable file type has no policy-defined domain
# transition, and returns an error BEFORE fork -- this is a policy-computation
# check, not an AVC decision, so Permissive does not bypass it. u:r:su:s0 is
# chosen because this device is userdebug + Permissive, where the `su` domain
# exists. Override via SUD_SECLABEL at install time if that domain is not
# present on a given device.
#
# Not oneshot on purpose: init auto-restarts a non-oneshot service ~5s after
# it dies, so sud comes back on its own if it ever crashes.
#
# A wrong or unknown seclabel just means init logs an error and the service
# never starts; boot continues normally either way, never a brick.

service sud /system/xbin/sud
    class late_start
    user root
    seclabel u:r:su:s0
